## Interpretation and evidence

Selected actions, flags, deadlines, and document quality checks describe the
configured assessment. They do not establish that supplied statements are true,
that a control is effective, or that a workflow complies with a law, standard,
or contract. The demonstration evidence records a synthetic example.

This output is not legal advice, official guidance, an endorsement by an authority,
or a certification of compliance. Use appropriate reviewers to assess the rules,
evidence, and conclusions before relying on them for a real workflow.

## Integrity and distribution

The assessment fingerprint identifies conclusions; the
[file inventory](CHECKSUMS.sha256) identifies delivered bytes. Sealing verifies
that inventory and declared evidence requirements. An unsigned seal does not
identify a signer, and a signature does not certify the correctness of the content.

